    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="20.8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 20.8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ætwinde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, ⁊ hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.2"/> hwa feormige, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.3"/> he his weres scyldig, buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.4"/> he hine ladian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.5"/> durre be þæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.6"/> flyman were, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine flyman nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.8" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif he ðonne oþwinde, ⁊ hwa hine feormige, sy his weres scyldig, butan he hine ladian durre be ðæs flyman were, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hine flymene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1"/> nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="20.8" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="162" ed="#liebermann"/>. . . inde, ⁊ hine hwa feormige, sie he . . ., . . n he hine ladian durre be þæs . . ., . . flemne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-4"/> nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="20.8" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="163" ed="#liebermann"/>Si aufugerit, et eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-3"/> aliquis (interim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.2-2"/>) firmauerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.3-2"/>, were sue sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.4-2"/> reus, nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.5-2"/> se possit idoneare secundum ipsius profugi weram, quod eum nesciebat flyman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.6-2"/> (id est fugitiuum) esse.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="20.8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="138" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif he ætwinde<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_20-8.attnote.fn.8"/>, ⁊ hine hwa feormige, sy he his weres scyldig, buton he hine ladian durre be þæs flyman were, þæt he hine flyman<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_20-8.attnote.fn.9"/> nyste.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="163" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn er (aber <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>) entflieht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.1"/>, und ihn jemand beherbergt, sei dieser das Wergeld jenes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.2"/> schuldig, ausser wenn er sich mit [Eid in Höhe vom] Wergeld des Geächteten rein zu schwören<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.3"/> wagt, dass er ihn nicht als Geächteten kannte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If (however, Ld) he escapes, and someone harbours him, let that person be liable for his wergild, unless he dares to clear himself with [an oath to the amount of] the outlaw's wergild that he did not know him to be an outlaw.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="139" ed="#attenborough"/>If he escapes and anyone harbours him, he [who does so] shall forfeit his<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_20-8.attnote.n.1"/> wergeld unless he dares to clear himself by [declaring on an oath equal to] the fugitive’s wergeld, that he did not know he was a fugitive.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="422" ed="#whitelock"/>If he escapes, and anyone harbours him, he is to be liable to pay his wergild, unless he dares to clear himself by the [amount of the] fugitive’s wergild, that he did not know that he was a fugitive.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_13-2">II Cn 13.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><ref target="clause:IICn_13-2">II Cn 13.2</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æt <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æt on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hwa hi., <hi rend="italic">durch Zeichen umgestellt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hwa hi., transposed by marks</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ein Buchstabe vor</hi> an <hi rend="italic">radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a letter erased before an</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæs f. w. þ. <hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæs f. w. þ. in the margin</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> a. e. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; a. e. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> -mabit <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; -mabit the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. sit <hi rend="italic">MHkBr;</hi> r. erit <hi rend="italic">RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. sit MHkBr; r. erit RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ni <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ni K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">163</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">flyemæn <hi rend="italic">Or;</hi> fliman <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">flyemæn Or; fliman T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">162</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Archetyp stand <hi rend="italic">oðwinde,</hi> was erst Hcorr. änderte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The archetype had <hi rend="italic">oðwinde,</hi> which was not altered until Hcorr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Des Geächteten (so auch Schmid 145. 575; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3. 14; Gefährdeeid 4). Denn die Eidesschwere (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2 b) entspricht der Höhe des abzuwendenden Strafgelds</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Of the outlaw (so also Schmid 145. 575; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 3. 14; Gefährdeeid 4). For the weight of the oath (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2 b) corresponds to the amount of the fine to be averted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">idoneare</hi> Frankolatein für <hi rend="italic">purgare, s. Wb.</hi> [Sondersinn: ‘Wahrheit gescholtener Urkunde erhärten’: Brunner II 421]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">idoneare</hi> is Frankish Latin for <hi rend="italic">purgare</hi>, see <hi rend="italic">Wb.</hi> [Special sense: ‘to establish the truth of a challenged charter’: Brunner II 421]</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">‘his’ refers to the fugitive.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">138</biblScope></bibl><label>ætwinde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">ðonne oþwinde</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_20-8.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">138</biblScope></bibl><label>flyman</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">flymene</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
